  "snapshot_notes": [
    "Some official pages are living status pages. Each corpus document records the publication-time state represented by its timestamp, not the page's current state.",
    "Where an official correction or amendment changed an earlier release, the corpus preserves separate time-scoped paraphrases and labels the correction relationship; it does not silently replace history.",
    "Translated and non-English-source cases are independently paraphrased and marked as such; no machine-translated article text is stored.",
    "Post-cutoff 2026 cases reduce, but cannot eliminate, the possibility that a model knows historical families from pretraining. The set is implementation-blind, not guaranteed pretraining-blind."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The collection is deliberately adversarial and structurally balanced, not an estimate of production news prevalence.",
    "Official-source selection creates an institutional-source bias and underrepresents local and investigative reporting.",
    "The set is English-heavy despite multilingual and translated-source traps.",
    "Manual labels encode one documented editorial policy; ambiguity should be surfaced through abstention analysis rather than hidden.",
    "A strong result on one sealed set does not establish generality; a fresh collection period and unseen families are required for replication."
  ]
